prompt:
You are contributing to TaskForge, a TypeScript + Bun CLI used in the RazorCascade memory reliability study.

Execution mode: cascade
Standardized task: 5. Gate summarizer integration
Objective: Compress the history into a structured summary before flagship execution.

Context from prior work:
Goal: Implement `cascade complete <id>` and `cascade delete <id>` commands with robust validation and user feedback.
Decisions: Use `commander.js` for CLI parsing and command definition.; Define a `Task` interface with `id`, `status`, `title`, `priority`, and `tags`.; Implement atomic JSON file persistence using `Bun.file()` for I/O.; Support `cascade list` with filters for status, priority, tags, and free-text search.; Implement `cascade complete <id>` and `cascade delete <id>` using a read-modify-write pattern.
Risks: Schema evolution will require a migration strategy for existing data.; Performance bottleneck for large task sets due to in-memory filtering.; Race conditions with concurrent CLI executions writing to the same file.
